%% Reconciled against shipped code as of task 4.28 (Phase 4 exit gate). This diagram shows what
%% `meridian tui` actually does today, not the original T17 design's aspiration — see
%% tui-client.md's "Current implementation status (as of 4.28)" section for the full writeup this
%% diagram is the picture of. Two things are load-bearing and easy to miss from the diagram shape
%% alone, so they are called out again here:
%% 1. `apps/tui/src/lib.rs::run_worker` is still an inert stub (unchanged since task 4.11's own
%%    placeholder scope): it echoes every dispatched `Effect` straight back as
%%    `WorkerEvent::Completed` with no outcome populated, never calling `meridian-core`. A real
%%    session therefore cannot progress past Onboarding's "Generating identity" step — confirmed
%%    empirically (4.28): the TUI hangs indefinitely on "please wait…" once the org hint is
%%    submitted. `Ctrl-Q` still quits and restores the terminal cleanly from that stuck state.
%% 2. There is no `Preflight` routing step and no `Screen::Main`. `App::new()` unconditionally
%%    starts on `Screen::Onboarding`; onboarding's own completion swaps to a bare
%%    `Screen::Placeholder`, never a real "Main" screen, because none exists. `Screen::Unlock`,
%%    `Contacts`, `ContactDetail`, `Chat`, `Verify`, and `Settings` are each fully built and
%%    unit-tested (`ratatui::backend::TestBackend`) but are reachable in this crate's own tests only
%%    by constructing them directly and pushing them onto the stack — nothing in
%%    `App::handle_key`/`App::handle_worker` ever pushes any of them during a live run.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Launch

  Launch --> EnvGate: meridian tui
  EnvGate --> Bail: not a TTY / TERM=dumb / smaller than 80x24
  Bail --> [*]: print the equivalent headless CLI command, exit 1
  note right of EnvGate
    Real and tested (apps/cli/src/tui.rs::check_environment).
    The one part of this whole diagram that is both live-wired
    AND reachable exactly as designed.
  end note

  EnvGate --> Onboarding: environment OK, always (no Preflight routing step exists)

  state Onboarding {
    [*] --> ChooseStore
    ChooseStore --> OrgHint: OS keystore or passphrase keyfile
    OrgHint --> Generating: enter the @domain hint
    Generating --> ShowIdentity: GenerateAccount effect resolves
    ShowIdentity --> Registering: connect to rendezvous, optional invite token
    Registering --> PublishingBundle: registered
    PublishingBundle --> [*]: prekey bundle published
    note right of Generating
      NEVER RESOLVES in a real run today — see this
      file's header note (1). The sub-step machine
      itself is real (task 4.16); only the worker
      executing its Effect is missing.
    end note
  }

  Onboarding --> Help: F1 (global, wired — reachable even while stuck on Generating)
  Help --> Onboarding: Esc
  Onboarding --> Palette: Ctrl-K (global, wired — reachable even while stuck on Generating)
  Palette --> Onboarding: Esc or run a registered command
  Onboarding --> Requests: Ctrl-R (global, wired — reachable even while stuck on Generating)
  Requests --> Onboarding: Esc
  note right of Onboarding
    F1 / Ctrl-K / Ctrl-R are checked unconditionally in
    App::handle_key before any per-screen dispatch, so they
    reach Help/Palette/Requests from EVERY screen, not just
    Placeholder — confirmed live even while stuck on
    Generating's "please wait…" step. The edges here and on
    Placeholder are the same three global chords, drawn
    twice only because those are the two states this diagram
    otherwise shows; treat them as always-available, not
    Placeholder/Onboarding-specific.
  end note

  Onboarding --> Placeholder: onboarding finished (only reachable if Generating's worker gap above is fixed)
  note right of Placeholder
    Screen::Placeholder is a bare "screen content lands in
    later tasks" stand-in. Screen::Main does not exist.
  end note

  Placeholder --> [*]: Ctrl-Q, global, wired, confirmed the terminal is restored cleanly, incl. from a stuck Onboarding screen
  Placeholder --> Help: F1 (global, wired)
  Help --> Placeholder: Esc
  Placeholder --> Palette: Ctrl-K (global, wired)
  Palette --> Placeholder: Esc or run a registered command
  Palette --> Diagnostics: Diagnostics, the one command registered at startup today
  Diagnostics --> Placeholder: Esc
  Placeholder --> Requests: Ctrl-R, global, wired, always pushes an EMPTY queue, no live chat session to snapshot pending requests from
  Requests --> Placeholder: Esc

  state "Fully built and screen-snapshot-tested, reached ONLY by direct construction in this crate's own tests, no live route from Onboarding or Placeholder exists anywhere in the app's key/worker dispatch" as NotLiveWired {
    Unlock
    Contacts
    ContactDetail
    Chat
    Verify
    Settings

    Contacts --> ContactDetail: Enter on a contact (this one screen-to-screen edge is really wired, once Contacts is on the stack at all)
    ContactDetail --> Contacts: Esc
    note right of Contacts
      "Enter" opens ContactDetail, never a chat screen —
      Screen::Chat exists and is fully wired but nothing
      pushes it from here. "v" shows a "Verify is not
      implemented yet (task 4.22) — press v again to
      dismiss" stand-in notice instead of pushing
      Screen::Verify, which also exists and is fully wired,
      just not reachable from here.
    end note

    note right of Chat
      Composer send-gate logic (Ok / Warn / Blocked, per
      meridian_core::trust::TrustStore::can_send) is real
      and adversarially tested (task 4.23): a verified
      contact's key change disables the composer with the
      canonical verification-ux.md wording, no dismiss-
      without-verify path. Only the SCREEN's own internal
      logic is proven — Chat itself is never pushed by a
      live run (see the "NotLiveWired" note above).
    end note

    note right of Verify
      Same story as Chat: mark-verified / block / acknowledge
      and the two un-softenable key-change banners are real,
      reviewed T08-primitive-backed logic (task 4.22), proven
      via TestBackend snapshots — just never reached from a
      live run.
    end note
  }
